{
  "requirement": "The bundled skills MUST direct agents to write site queries that select every place the obligation applies and no others, violation queries for every kind of construct that could break it, and, for every query, `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has three directive obligations, and the single marked test covers each.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. The skills direct agents to write site queries that select every place the obligation applies and no others.\n2. They direct agents to write violation queries for every kind of construct that could break the obligation.\n3. They direct agents to give every query `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions.\n\n**Test**\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_direct_exact_site_queries_violation_queries_and_snippets]` reads the `## Do` section of the habeas skill's `references/distributed-requirements.md`. It does this through the helpers `distributed_reference`, `section` and `assert_text`. `section` collapses whitespace, so phrases that wrap across lines in the markdown still match. `assert_text` asserts that the section contains four phrases:\n- \"check that the site queries select every place the obligation applies and no others\" covers obligation 1, both \"every place\" and \"no others\".\n- \"Write a violation query, with `within` naming the site query, for every kind of construct that could break the obligation\" covers obligation 2.\n- \"Give every query `match` and `no_match` snippets that test its conditions\" covers obligation 3's \"every query\" and both snippet kinds.\n- \"This applies to violation queries too.\" shows that the snippet obligation also applies to violation queries.\n\nI read the skill text, and it contains these phrases in the `Do` section's bullets. Each assertion fails if its sentence is dropped or weakened, so none passes vacuously.\n\n**Remaining questions**\nThe requirement says \"bundled skills\", but the test checks only the habeas skill's distributed-requirements reference. That reference is the topic home for this guidance, and other skills refer to it. I did not find a separate required direction in another skill that would need its own test. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply, and I found no gaps.",
